unityrs-imageio ports Pillow 9.5.0's PNG writer as Image.save(fp, "PNG")
runs it at its defaults, so its PNG files are Pillow's byte for byte:
crates/unityrs-imageio/src/png.rs translates src/PIL/PngImagePlugin.py's
_save, putchunk and _idat, src/PIL/ImageFile.py's _save and _encode_tile,
and the encode loop of src/libImaging/ZipEncode.c;
crates/unityrs-imageio/src/filter.rs translates ZipEncode.c's choice of each
row's PNG filter; crates/unityrs-imageio/src/hash.rs translates the
converters of convert("RGBA") in src/libImaging/Convert.c (l2rgb, la2rgb,
rgb2rgba).

crates/unityrs-texture/src/bcn.rs translates Pillow 9.5.0's BC1, BC2, BC3,
BC4, BC5 and BC7 block decoders to Rust (src/libImaging/BcnDecode.c:
decode_565, decode_bc1_color, decode_bc3_alpha, decode_bc2_block,
decode_bc4_block, decode_bc5_block, decode_bc7_block with the tables it
reads, and the block order of put_block and decode_bcn), so that a DXT1,
DXT3, DXT5, BC4, BC5 or BC7 texture decodes to the pixels UnityPy 1.25.2
gets from Pillow 9.5.0. BcnDecode.c's own header dedicates that file to the
public domain (CC0); the port keeps the notice of the release it comes from
all the same. crates/unityrs-texture/src/raw.rs ports Pillow 9.5.0's raw
decoder as UnityPy 1.25.2 calls it (src/libImaging/RawDecode.c's row loop,
and src/libImaging/Unpack.c's unpackers for the raw modes UnityPy names:
band0, band3, ImagingUnpackBGR, unpackBGRA, unpackARGB, ImagingUnpackBGR16
and ImagingUnpackRGBA4B); crates/unityrs-texture/src/decode.rs the width
cap of src/decode.c's _setimage and the decompression-bomb check of
src/PIL/Image.py's crop, with its message.
crates/unityrs-texture/src/sprite/ ports what UnityPy 1.25.2's SpriteHelper
calls of Pillow 9.5.0: canvas.rs the crop (src/PIL/Image.py's crop and _crop,
src/libImaging/Crop.c), the transposes (src/libImaging/Geometry.c),
Image.merge's size check and the width cap every image Pillow makes passes
(src/libImaging/Storage.c's ImagingNewPrologueSubtype); raster.rs the
polygon fill of ImageDraw.polygon (src/libImaging/Draw.c's
ImagingDrawPolygon, add_edge, polygon_generic, hline8, x_cmp and the
ROUND_UP and ROUND_DOWN macros, and src/_imaging.c's _draw_polygon);
affine.rs the nearest-neighbour affine transform (Geometry.c's
ImagingTransformAffine, ImagingScaleAffine, check_fixed and affine_fixed);
and render.rs Image.new's size check,
paste, putalpha and composite (src/PIL/Image.py, src/libImaging/Paste.c).

