crates/unityrs-texture/src/etc.rs translates texture2ddecoder 1.0.5's ETC
and EAC block decoders to Rust (src/Texture2DDecoder/etc.cpp:
decode_etc1_block, decode_etc2_block, decode_etc2a1_block,
decode_etc2a8_block, decode_eac_block, decode_eac_signed_block, the tables
they read, and the block loops decode_etc1 to decode_eacrg_signed with
src/Texture2DDecoder/color.h's copy_block_buffer), so that an ETC_RGB4,
ETC2_RGB, ETC2_RGBA1, ETC2_RGBA8, EAC_R, EAC_R_SIGNED, EAC_RG or
EAC_RG_SIGNED texture decodes to the pixels UnityPy 1.25.2 gets from it,
but for one Tier C change (ETC2_RGBA1's transparent pixels, PARITY.md
section 19.1). The source is the release's sdist (texture2ddecoder-1.0.5.tar.gz,
sha256 7767e865394ad8e0a0609d275caf3e8c99d03df107dfb961cb90ea21c9295dc2),
whose LICENSE follows first. texture2ddecoder wraps the decoders of
AssetStudio's Texture2DDecoderNative (its README says so), whose etc.cpp
its own matches but for casts, and that file matches mikunyan's
ext/decoders/native/etc.c nearly line for line; neither file carries a
notice of its own, so the notices of all three projects, each MIT, follow,
AssetStudio's and mikunyan's from their repositories' LICENSE files. They
are unityrs-texture's LICENSE-TEXTURE2DDECODER, LICENSE-ASSETSTUDIO and
LICENSE-MIKUNYAN, listed under MIT below.

