crates/unityrs-texture/src/sprite/affine.rs ports the order in which
OpenBLAS 0.3.31's Haswell kernels solve a 6 x 6 system for numpy's
linalg.solve (interface/lapack/gesv.c, lapack/getrf/getrf_single.c,
lapack/getf2/getf2_k.c, lapack/getrs/getrs_single.c,
lapack/laswp/generic/laswp_k_4.c, driver/level2/trsv_L.c and trsv_U.c, and
the x86_64 kernels ddot.c, dgemv_n_4.c with dgemv_n_microk_haswell-4.c,
daxpy.c, dscal.c and iamax_sse2.S), so that a sprite's affine triangle is
solved bit for bit as UnityPy 1.25.2's numpy solves it. Three notices
follow, each listed under BSD-3-Clause below:
- OpenBLAS's LICENSE, unityrs-texture's LICENSE-OPENBLAS, the licence of
  all of those files;
- the notice that ddot.c, dgemv_n_4.c, dgemv_n_microk_haswell-4.c and
  daxpy.c each carry (2014, and a disclaimer naming the OpenBLAS project),
  unityrs-texture's LICENSE-OPENBLAS-KERNELS;
- the notice dscal.c carries (2013 - 2015), unityrs-texture's
  LICENSE-OPENBLAS-DSCAL.
The other files, from GotoBLAS2, carry The University of Texas at Austin's
notice instead (the next section).

